ng and build validation.\n\nNow I'm looking at the next task which focuses on implementing requirement R4.3 specifically, modifying both the main implementation and test files to add differential test coverage for this new requirement. R1\n        text: \"Implement srd076 requirement R4.3 per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Add differential test cases covering R4.3 using testutils.RunDiffTests against gb2sum reference binary\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use pkg/hashutil for shared hash computation and checksum formatting\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the differential testing pattern: testutils.BuildBinary for Go binary, exec.LookPath for gb2sum reference, t.Skip if reference not found\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Preserve existing implementation structure from prior tasks (R1.1-R4.2)\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/b2sum/... passes with no warnings\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go build -o bin/b2sum ./cmd/b2sum/ succeeds\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/b2sum/... -count=1 passes (or skips gracefully if gb2sum not in PATH)\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"srd076 R4.3 is implemented and all b2sum requirements are complete\"\n\nNow I'm moving on to the next task: implementing the cksum command per srd077, starting with requirements R1.1 through R1.4. I'll need to review the cksum specification, examine the shared hash utilities, and study the existing checksum utility patterns from md5sum and sha256sum as reference implementations. I'm setting up the cksum utility implementation with differential tests against the gcksum reference binary, handling SIGPIPE signals to match GNU coreutils behavior, and ensuring all four SRD requirements pass their acceptance criteria including build verification and test execution with proper environment configuration.\n\nNow moving to the sha384sum task, which requires implementing additional fu